proposal per millisecond, 4000 proposals) so that the two unread nodes keep observing transitions until they reach the bound; it waits up to 90s for both to stop answering commands, then measures whether the \\\"\n   \\\"healthy node 1 can still decide: it emits CA_EVENT default_capacity_parked_cluster {event_capacity,nodes_parked,decided_before,decided_after,append_notify_timeout_reached} and asserts that both unread nodes parked, that node 1 stayed \\\"\n   \\\"responsive, that its decided index was unchanged across the attempt, and that at least 1024 transitions had been observed before the two nodes parked (so the bound really was the default rather than a smaller configured one).\\\"),\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":(\\\"Bound measurement at the shipped default event capacity: does an unconsumed event stream park nodes and stall the cluster when the capacity is left at 1024?\\\"),\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"in-process 3-node cluster, majority quorum, in-process transport under harness control\\\",\\\"only node 1 consumes its event stream; nodes 2 and 3 leave the handle's receiver unread\\\",\\\"writes are paced at one per millisecond so consecutive decided-index changes are observed in separate ticks\\\"],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"deployments whose clients always drain events\\\",\\\"any latency claim about how long a real cluster needs to reach 1024 transitions\\\"],\n   \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":3,\\\"event_capacity\\\":\\\"RuntimeConfig::default() = 1024\\\",\\\"paced_proposals\\\":4000,\\\"wait_s\\\":90}},\n },\n}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
